. Along with generating responses, I worked on tracking how many input and output tokens were used, how much time the request took and the estimated cost of using the API. I also added a retry option so that the program can try again if a temporary error occurs. MongoDB was used to store the usage details, including the model name, provider, token count and request status. I also wrote test cases to check the working of the program. Through this experiment, I learned how to monitor API usage, estimate costs and handle errors.
